   "t": 1791261383.786895,
   "kind": "assistant_text",
   "text": "The stop trigger fired as declared, confirming the single-feature specification [29-] (feature 29, short) achieved an in-sample Sharpe of 1.4409, well above my 1.2 bar. This is a single feature, which is simple, interpretable, and already strong \u2014 consistent with my pre-registered stopping rule, so I'll finalize here rather than risk overfitting with additional combination moves.\n\nNow let me form my out-of-sample Sharpe prediction. In-sample Sharpe of 1.4 for a single feature (not an overfit 3-feature combination search) typically degrades out-of-sample due to:\n- Selection bias (I picked the best of 80 candidates via `init`)\n- Regime change / non-stationarity\n- The feature being single (less diversified, more fragile to its own idiosyncratic decay)\n\nA reasonable haircut for \"best of 80\" single-feature selection is substantial \u2014 often 30-50% Sharpe decay is observed in these settings, with meaningful uncertainty."
